        "id": "practice",
        "title": "Manufacturing practice",
        "html": "<p>A major assembly carries its national manufacturer plate, regional or provincial device, contractor identification and Community certification. Small engraved or stamped shields appear behind service panels; larger visible assemblies can bear painted marks. Acceptance records connect the symbol to lots, inspection and configuration records.</p><p>The marks assist responsibility, recall tracing, failure investigation and replacement routing. They supplement serial numbers and technical documentation. They do not replace those records.</p>"
